WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.520
In 2026, a woman became Archbishop
of Canterbury for the first time.

2
00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:10.780
Yet one of Paul's letters says: let
the wives be quiet in the assemblies.

3
00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:14.240
Christians have argued about
that one line for centuries,

4
00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:15.590
and still do.

5
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:18.820
One verse, read in very different ways.

6
00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.670
Why do Christians read it so differently?

7
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.540
In this mission, you'll meet
women Paul names in Romans 16,

8
00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.870
among them Phoebe and Junia.

9
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.390
Then you'll follow women
leaders through history,

10
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.690
and compare the Churches today.

11
00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:37.150
Your mission: find out why Christians
read this verse so differently.
